// S45 (d) twin (3)/(4), variant M: the same contract without the requires "every a[i] < 100": the overflow obligation of a[i] + 1 under the binder fails at its row, alone: the failed row is assumed afterwards (as every failed row is), and the later unquantified clause (a[0] + 1), which rested on the same fact, then passes: one error.
